      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T19:18:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I just wanted to point out that this type of thing should not be considered a Robolectric bug, as it was a libcore + framework change, and could have impacts elsewhere (e.g. layoutlib).\n\nPerhaps there\u0027s a bit of a blame overload to calling it a \u0027Robolectric bug\u0027. I didn\u0027t mean Robolectric caused the issue, but rather just that it\u0027s Robolectric\u0027s problem to fix it anyway (such as via rewrite operations, as was submitted). It falls into a similar category to \"framework changed something and now Robolectric needs to track that update\" that happens with some degree of frequency.",
